children.desc:
The deviation by a prism depends on four things:

- the **angle of incidence** (see the curve);
- the **material**: a bigger μ gives more deviation. **Flint glass** deviates more than **crown glass**;
- the **angle of the prism A**: a bigger A gives more deviation;
- the **colour**: **violet is deviated most, red least**.

It does **not** depend on the **size** of the prism.

**Worked example:** white light goes into a prism. Violet has the biggest μ, so it turns most. Red turns least. The colours spread out: you will meet this again in the chapter on the spectrum.
